     "text": "**Discrete Boundary Split Trap at $n=0$!**\nWhen computing $h[n] = s[n] - s[n-1]$ where $s[n] = \\alpha^n u[n]$:\n- For $n = 0$: $h[0] = s[0] - s[-1] = \\alpha^0 (1) - 0 = 1$.\n- For $n \\ge 1$: $h[n] = \\alpha^n - \\alpha^{n-1} = \\alpha^n(1 - \\alpha^{-1})$.\nExpressing $h[n]$ compactly requires isolating the Kronecker delta at $n=0$:\n$$h[n] = \\delta[n] + (\\alpha - 1)\\alpha^{n-1} u[n-1]$$\nNever carelessly write $(\\alpha^n - \\alpha^{n-1})u[n]$, because at $n=0$ that formula incorrectly evaluates to $1 - \\alpha^{-1} \\ne 1$!"
